 "notes": [
  "1976 police station: brown cladding panels with two-light ribbon windows on the first and second floors; the street front (west, Van Leijenberghlaan) has a solid ground floor; east, south and courtyard walls have a third ribbon at ground level.",
  "Entrance: a projecting glass box (its own 3DBAG volume, surface 7) two storeys tall, POLITIE lettered on the frosted glass of the upper half (2016 and 2019 panoramas); modelled as a two-storey glazed entrance hall with glazing-mounted lettering.",
  "The north wing is grey exposed concrete (2025 north panorama) with the same ribbons; the 3DBAG west plane spans both the grey and the brown part, so the west wall stays brown.",
  "Police components not used: no striped band, blue lamp, canopy or garage doors are visible in the 2016/2019/2025 panoramas; rooftop stair/lift cores are 3DBAG volumes already (roofPlant off).",
  "Sides of the entrance box (surfaces 46, 52) and rooftop volumes stay blank (otherWalls).",
  "Measured 2026-10-14 (measure.ts, evidence in measured.json): groups 0, 2, 4 take the photo's wall and glass colour, window shape, bay count and front class; walls[0] glass #403535 not used (not darker than the wall #5b4b44 by 10 L*, or tinted): kit glass kept; walls[2] glass #3b3732 not used (not darker than the wall #493d32 by 10 L*, or tinted): kit glass kept; walls[4] glass #395455 not used (not darker than the wall #5e5855 by 10 L*, or tinted): kit glass kept."
